From 0578e7113d3f7f2e39d89459925faf3ec1281dd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cyril Moron <cyril.moron@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:56:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: bound the sender queue and open per-topic QoS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A client reading slower than publishers publish grew the outgoing FIFO
without limit — memory, and worse, ever-staler frames on screen. State
streams only need the latest sample; commands need lossless FIFO. Two
opt-in ROS parameters, empty by default so behavior is unchanged:

- COALESCE_TOPICS: comma-separated regexes; matching topics keep at most
  one pending frame in the sender queue (drop-stale, keep-latest).
- BEST_EFFORT_TOPICS: matching subscriptions use BEST_EFFORT/VOLATILE/
  KEEP_LAST(1) instead of the hardcoded RELIABLE/TRANSIENT_LOCAL(1000)
  (a BEST_EFFORT subscriber under a RELIABLE publisher is valid DDS).

Coalescing lives in a stdlib-only module, unit-tested without rclpy.
